  "note": "Annual election of one third of the Portstewart Urban District Council, polled Monday 16 January 1928. Seven candidates were nominated for four seats; one withdrew before the poll, leaving six. The Irish News prints the result. Thomas Lennox, one of the seven nominated, does not appear in the poll and presumably withdrew."
